schema and name are required

# an implicit (AS-less) attribute alias cannot shadow a canonical column either: the regex
# refusal only sees "AS _x", so the compiled projection is described and the displaced
# duplicate (_size_1) is the proof
statement error
CALL tree_ddl_create('main', 'bad10', tree_spec(tree_shape("order" := 'node_id', level := 'depth', semantic := tree_semantic(attr := 'CAST(depth AS BIGINT) _size, name')), source := 'read_parquet(''test/data/app.parquet'')'));
----
shadows a canonical column: _size

# ... and so does every OTHER canonical column. The check's alternation used to be a
# hand-written list of the thirteen names, and only _size was ever exercised (FINDINGS said
# so); the catalog's vocabulary renames then left it naming `id`, `classes` and `pseudo` while
# the projection emitted _key, _tags and _predicate, so a source column called _key, _tags or
# _predicate DISPLACED the canonical column and this check -- the one whose whole job is to
# catch that -- said nothing. One record per canonical column, so no arm is untested again.
#
# The shadow column is typed BIGINT on purpose. A VARCHAR one makes the projection's own
# arithmetic over _pre, _level and _size fail to BIND first (No function matches '+(VARCHAR,
# INTEGER_LITERAL)'), which refuses for the wrong reason and would not exercise the regex;
# measured both ways.

statement error
CALL tree_ddl_create('main', 'bad_shadow_root', tree_spec(tree_shape(root := 'file_path', "order" := 'node_id', level := 'depth'), source := '(SELECT *, 1::BIGINT AS "_root" FROM read_parquet(''test/data/app.parquet''))'));
----
shadows a canonical column: _root

statement error
CALL tree_ddl_create('main', 'bad_shadow_pre', tree_spec(tree_shape(root := 'file_path', "order" := 'node_id', level := 'depth'), source := '(SELECT *, 1::BIGINT AS "_pre" FROM read_parquet(''test/data/app.parquet''))'));
----
shadows a canonical column: _pre

statement error
